    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1499">

                <pb facs="1298" n="1040" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1040"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/322</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-11T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 11, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.15 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2986. My 2736, September 3, and your 2088, September 9, 5 p. m., and September
                    13, p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1499-f1"/> The plan is scotched apparently for
                    good by objections from the French Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1499-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1499-f1-content">
                <p>Instruction of September 13 not printed.</p>
